---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import BreadcrumbDemo from '../../components/BreadcrumbDemo';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<Docs title="Breadcrumb" description="A path of links that shows where a page or folder sits.">
  <h1 class="docs-title">Breadcrumb</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A path of links that shows where a page or folder sits. Seven small parts you compose yourself, with router links,
    button crumbs, hidden folders, and one-line trails.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8">
    <BreadcrumbDemo client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Breadcrumb usage"
      code={`import {
  Breadcrumb,
  BreadcrumbEllipsis,
  BreadcrumbItem,
  BreadcrumbLink,
  BreadcrumbList,
  BreadcrumbPage,
  BreadcrumbSeparator,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/breadcrumb";

<Breadcrumb aria-label="Folder path">
  <BreadcrumbList>
    <BreadcrumbItem>
      <BreadcrumbLink render={<Link to="/files" />}>All files</BreadcrumbLink>
    </BreadcrumbItem>
    <BreadcrumbSeparator />
    <BreadcrumbItem>
      <BreadcrumbEllipsis />
      <span className="sr-only">Folders you cannot open</span>
    </BreadcrumbItem>
    <BreadcrumbSeparator />
    <BreadcrumbItem>
      <BreadcrumbPage truncate>{folder.name}</BreadcrumbPage>
    </BreadcrumbItem>
  </BreadcrumbList>
</Breadcrumb>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>Breadcrumb</code> is a <code>nav</code>. Its label defaults to "Breadcrumb"; pass <code>aria-label</code>{' '}
      for paths such as "Folder path" or "Destination path". <code>BreadcrumbList</code> is an ordered list,
      <code>BreadcrumbItem</code> a list item, and <code>BreadcrumbSeparator</code>a hidden list item with a chevron.
      Pass children to the separator to use another icon.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Links and buttons</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Breadcrumb render"
      code={`<BreadcrumbLink href="/home">
  <Home aria-hidden="true" />
  Home
</BreadcrumbLink>

<BreadcrumbLink
  truncate
  render={<Button variant="ghost" size="xs" disabled={moving} onClick={open} />}
>
  {folder.name}
</BreadcrumbLink>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>BreadcrumbLink</code> renders an <code>a</code>. The Base UI <code>render</code> prop swaps it for your
      router's link or a Sprõut <code>Button</code>, such as a ghost <code>xs</code> button inside a picker that does
      not change the URL. A leading icon is sized to 14px. <code>BreadcrumbPage</code> marks the current step with{' '}
      <code>aria-current="page"</code> and is not clickable.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Long names and one-line trails</h2>
    <p>
      Set <code>truncate</code> on a link or page to cut a long name to one line with an ellipsis. String names also get
      a <code>title</code> with the full name. The width is 12rem; set <code>--sprout-breadcrumb-label-width</code>
      on any parent to change it.
    </p>
    <p>
      The list wraps by default. <code>wrap=&#123;false&#125;</code> keeps it on one line, as in an app header: every
      step keeps its width, and the item with <code>aria-current="page"</code> shrinks. Put the page heading inside that
      item and truncate it.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      <code>BreadcrumbEllipsis</code> and separators are hidden from screen readers. Put the reason in a visually hidden
      sibling, for example "Higher folders not shown", "Loading folder path", or "Folder path unavailable". Loading
      spinners, retries, and error messages belong to your application. Links show a focus ring. Separators flip in
      right-to-left text. Color changes last 120ms and stop when reduced motion is requested.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Steps use <code>--sprout-muted</code>, the current page and hovered links use <code>--sprout-text</code>, and the
      focus ring uses <code>--sprout-focus</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
